**DAG-POOL does not repair the shared-descent gap.** The discriminant scaling \(Q^{(D-1)(D-2)}\), the \(D^{\omega(Q)}\) lattice count, and the additive pooled profile check out. The cusp budget also works under the stated size restriction. The missing step is a quota of **fresh smooth residuals**. Pairing rows \(q^3b_i\) with one eliminator \(qb_0\) can produce independent base relations while stripping the prescribed \(q\) leaves \(q^2b_i\) in every parent. [Full cross-review](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/hatch_h1c/cross_review.md)

**G-H1’s folded experiment survives blind recovery.** All 30 planted messages were recovered uniquely using all four equations. The theorem establishes affine-subspace containment. A coordinate-only argument gives the same leading threshold for a fixed field, so the Galois action is unnecessary for that guarantee. I also found an explicit polynomial that certifies a candidate below G-H1’s claimed universal `Int(Z)` wall. [Blind replay](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/hatch_h1c/review_check.out:2) · [Counterexample](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/hatch_h1c/cross_review.md:23)

**Accept into the repo as proved**

- DAG-POOL’s arithmetic lemmas and its model floor conditional on H and a fresh quota.
- TIED-PARITY’s local ranks, MIN-ROW, the repaired PIN laws, and single-target accounting. C-RM still lacks independent exceptional-norm yield.
- G-H1’s local jet identities, fixed-order determinant calculation, `Int(Z)` indices and covolume bound, affine containment, and primitive full-orbit obstruction.
- C-H1’s fixed-profile weighted Theorem J and C-H2’s determinant obstruction at a fixed height cutoff. [Disposition](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/hatch_h1c/cross_review.md:29)

**Single best next attack.** Bound how much independent base rank a shared descent can obtain from rows that introduce no fresh odd large-prime column. Charge repeated primes and even powers at their actual stripped divisors. That would address the precise implication DAG-POOL still needs.